  "basis": "The chart 'Urban Water Supply by Source' displays a clear conflict between the bar heights and the numeric labels. The 'Groundwater' bar is the tallest, reaching approximately 68 on the 'Reported supply share (%)' axis, while the 'Surface water' bar is shorter at approximately 40. However, the labels are inverted: 'Surface water' is labeled 41.2% and 'Groundwater' is labeled 29.8%. Record r1 is supported by the O/B checks, establishing that the bar geometry is the authoritative encoding of the contribution magnitude on the provided scale. Record r2 is refuted because the labels are inconsistent with the chart's quantitative axis. Following the supported reading that bar height represents the contribution, 'Groundwater' is the largest source. The routing criterion requires escalating the largest contribution source to review.",
  "option_label": "Route Groundwater to escalated contribution review"
}
